course: dictionary
lesson: 14856
title: Words of great joy
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how strongly someone feels. «The crowd gave the singer a rapturous welcome.» The crowd is not just pleased. They are so happy that their joy shows, and rapturous means full of great joy.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Cheering, clapping and welcoming all show that people are happy and excited. When you meet rapturous, look for the joy that is around it.
explain: The word comes from «rapture», which means very great joy. If you know rapture, you can often work out rapturous, the describing word for something full of that joy. Swap in very happy and check that your meaning still fits the sentence.
fact: Rapturous means full of great joy and excitement.
fact: «Rapturous applause» is clapping that is loud, long and full of joy.
fact: Rapturous means showing extreme delight, so it is stronger than happy.
fact: Rapturous is an adjective: it describes a noun, like a rapturous welcome or rapturous cheers.
fact: Rapture is the noun for very great joy. Rapturous can change to more rapturous and most rapturous when you compare things.
exercise: «The fans gave the team a rapturous welcome when they came home.» What does rapturous mean here? | Wet and muddy | Angry and cross | *Full of great joy | Quiet and sleepy
exercise: «The audience gave rapturous applause at the end of the concert.» What kind of applause is it? | *Full of great joy and excitement | Dull and short | Thin and quiet | Slow and sleepy
exercise: Rapturous comes from a noun. Which word is that noun? | rapper | *rapture | repeat | rupture
test: Toad imagines «rapturous crowds cheering him». Which word best matches rapturous? | Frightened | *Joyful and excited | Bored | Sleepy
test: Which sentence shows rapturous cheers? | The class sat in silent boredom | *The crowd roared with rapturous cheers when the band walked on | The old bridge was closed for repairs | The rain fell softly all afternoon
exam: Mia wrote: «The audience gave a rapturous standing ovation.» What does rapturous tell you about the audience? | They were lost in the dark | *They were full of great joy and delight | They were tired from the long walk | They were bored and wanted to leave
